    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0819" n="1653" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/556</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-15T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 15, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5909. For McFadden [From War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 375. Your 466, Embassy 4349, October 7, 11 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d691-f1"
                    /> We are happy to note that the Blockade appears to be satisfied with our views
                    as to place of holding Swiss negotiations as expressed in our <pb facs="0820"
                        n="1654" xml:id="pg1654"/> note to French High Commission,
                        Washington.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d691-f2"/> It would be entirely agreeable
                    to us that after negotiations here have been completed and agreement prepared,
                    it be sent to Paris to be contemporaneously ratified by the Associated
                    Governments and the Swiss Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
